                <pb facs="0152" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-11T10:00:00+08:00">January 11, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 11—1:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 10, noon. According to information emanating from military
                            headquarters Japanese planes on January 7th or 8th bombarded the Chinese
                            troops concentrated in Jehol Province approximately 50 kilometres north
                            of Suichung. Details of the incident are not known. The Japanese Fourth
                            Cavalry Brigade has been transferred to Suichung”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
